// error
// SPEC §10.5, #3976: `@json` is refused on a GENERIC class. Every judgment the
// synthesis makes is syntactic -- a field's JSON shape is read off its declared
// type node, before any Checker exists -- and a type parameter has no declared
// shape to read.
//
// Refused by name rather than left to fail: unrefused, `this.v.toJson()` on a
// `T` reaches lowering as E0092 "cannot lower a call whose callee does not
// resolve to a function" pointing at the field, and it fails that way even for
// an instantiation whose argument DOES carry `@json` -- so the error names
// neither the real rule nor a fix.
import { Json, JsonEntry } from "std/json"

@json class Box<T> {
  v: T,
}

fn main() {
  print("${Box<i64>{ v: 1 }.v}\n")
}
